The '''Private Island''' (also known as the '''Player's Island''' and '''Your Island''') is where all players begin their SkyBlock adventure. Players can build and break blocks freely here, allowing them to customize the island to their liking. They can also place [[Minions]] to harvest resources. Except on {{Gamemode|Stranded}} mode, players can also place [[Portals]] to quickly travel to some [[Public Island]] locations. Many players use their island primarily for function, but some create interesting or useful islands for others to visit.

== Initial Island State ==
When the player first creates their profile, they spawn on one of two floating islands in the Private Island. The first island consists of some grass, dirt, and stone with an oak tree on top. Players are told to do some simple tasks before making their way to the second island.

The second of the two islands contains the Hub Island Portal, {{NPCSprite|Jerry}}, a {{Item|Cobblestone Minion}}, and a small cave with a torch and a chest inside.  The chest contains a {{Item|Lava Bucket}}, a {{Item|Water Bucket}}, 3 {{Item|Bone Meal}}, 5 {{Item|Dirt}}, 7 {{Item|Grass}} and 8 {{Item|Cobblestone}}. Presumably, the {{Item|Lava Bucket}} and {{Item|Water Bucket}} are for a cobblestone generator, which is particularly useful on {{Gamemode|Stranded}} mode.

== Progression ==
Except on {{Gamemode|Stranded}} mode, after finishing the tasks for the first quest, the player is instructed to enter the portal on the second island to travel to the [[Hub Island]]. After entering the Hub Island portal for the first time, players are able to complete quests throughout the Hub and other [[locations]]. These locations allow the player to, among other things, level up [[Skills]] and [[Collections]].

On {{Gamemode|Stranded}} mode, the player is restricted to the {{Zone|Private Island}} and {{Zone|The Garden}} for the entirety of the game. The player will obtain items and progress without accessing public islands. There are several changes to make parts of the game's content obtainable.

== Mobs ==
After the first full night, mobs spawn naturally on the Private Island in areas where the light level is low enough. Mob spawning can be prevented in multiple ways:
* Using a {{Item|Repelling Candle}} prevents all mob spawns on the island.
* Placing {{Item|torch}}es or other light sources prevents monsters from spawning in areas with enough light.
* Using a {{Item|Day Saver}} and {{Item|Weather Node}} on the island makes it permanently day and sunny, which makes the surface of the island constantly illuminated by the sun, so hostile mobs can't spawn.

