== Restrictions ==
=== Island Size ===
<!-- NOTE to editors: Prior to a patch (see Changelog/2022/May 16), the game described the default island size as 160x160, but the actual limit was 161x161. The game now correctly describes the size as 161x161.
-->The default island size is 161 blocks by 161 blocks, but it can be increased with the Island Size [[Account & Profile Upgrades#Profile Upgrades|Profile Upgrade]]. Attempting to build outside these limits results in the message {{Red|You can't build any further in this direction!}}. If the player travels vertically above Y:296, they are teleported back to their spawn location and receive the message {{Red|Careful! You cannot travel too far away from the island!}}.

=== Redstone Restrictions ===
Since [[Changelog/2019/July 2|version 0.5]], redstone has been allowed on Player Islands, with strict limitations. Each island has a [[Redstone Meter]] that appears on the scoreboard when a redstone component, such as a lever, is activated. When the meter reaches 100%, redstone on the island is disabled for 10 seconds. Pistons can be placed, but cannot be activated. Minecarts are disabled due to performance issues and duplication exploits.

=== Placeable Blocks Limit ===
Certain placeable blocks are limited to {{Green|1,000}}. Known blocks with this limit include {{Item|Chest}}s and {{Item|Hopper}}s.

Blocks placed before the limit was introduced were not affected. If a player tries to place a block with it exceeding the limit, a message will show:
